  "published": "2026-10-01T11:45:40.703Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0: text in every script as Report Viewer draws it: Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Thai and the rest in the font Report Viewer falls back to, at that font's widths; Hebrew and Arabic right to left; Arabic and the Indic scripts shaped (HarfBuzz). Image output (PNG, TIFF, JPEG) laid out at Windows' pixel widths and line heights, so its pages end where Report Viewer's do. Cambria, Verdana, Tahoma, Georgia, Trebuchet MS and Consolas at their Windows widths. Underlines and strikethroughs in PDF and images. A chart, gauge or map its engine rejects shows Report Viewer's error box; chart text as GDI+ draws it, aliased where the chart has no background. PDFs keep the text a cell cuts off (found by a search), and have the report's exact page size. On Linux, the first render names the fontconfig package it needs. Details: https://ssrs2.net",
